{
  "_comment": "Phase 13 Part A — code-interpreter sandbox seccomp profile. Default action is ERRNO (default-deny): any syscall NOT in the allowlist below returns EPERM instead of executing. The allowlist is the compute subset a CPython + numpy/pandas/matplotlib/openpyxl workload needs. Networking syscalls (socket/socketpair/connect/bind/listen/accept/sendto/recvfrom/sendmsg/recvmsg/setsockopt/getsockopt/getpeername/getsockname/shutdown) are DELIBERATELY ABSENT so model-authored code cannot even create a socket — defence-in-depth on top of `--network none`. ptrace/mount/umount/pivot_root/chroot/reboot/kexec/init_module/bpf/keyctl/setns/unshare/process_vm_* are also absent so no sandbox self-escalation or introspection of other processes. Combined with --cap-drop ALL and --security-opt no-new-privileges this profile also renders the setuid/setgid family inert (kept in the list only so libc startup doesn't ERRNO-crash; no-new-privileges neuters them).",
  "defaultAction": "SCMP_ACT_ERRNO",
  "defaultErrnoRet": 1,
